## Acceptance criteria

- No manual trigger buttons exist anywhere — Demo Mode is single-toggle, fully automatic once enabled.
- Each auto-selected reading pushes through the exact same path `VitalsProvider` would use for real data — no special-cased UI logic downstream.
- Normal readings → dashboard/ring update only, no alert.
- Sudden abnormal (resting) → existing SOS flow, unmodified.
- Sudden abnormal (exercise) → new Health Check screen, 60s countdown, two explicit options.
- Ambiguous/Override reading → escalates straight to SOS despite exercise tag; override function is unit-testable in isolation.
- Timeout or "I need help" on Health Check escalates through the same call/SMS/location code path as Tier 1 — verify no duplicated escalation logic.
- The escalation SMS (both tiers) contains the existing generic message plus the specific vitals values that triggered the alert.
- "I'm OK" on either flow cleanly returns to monitoring with no residual alert state.
- Demo Mode requires explicit confirmation before it can be enabled.
- Cooldown reliably prevents a second real call/SMS from firing while one emergency is unresolved or was just resolved within the cooldown window.
- Demo Mode pauses scheduling entirely while an alert is active — never queues or stacks triggers.
- Demo Mode banner is visible any time simulated data is active.
- No orphaned timers/state when Demo Mode is toggled off or the app is backgrounded mid-alert.

